neer, uses a digital still camera to make a photo of his helmet visor during the mission's third session of extravehicular activity (EVA). During the six-hour, 28-minute spacewalk, Hoshide and NASA astronaut <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunita_Williams\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Sunita Williams\">Sunita Williams</a> (visible in the reflections of Hoshide's helmet visor), flight engineer, completed the installation of a Main Bus Switching Unit (MBSU) that was hampered last week by a possible misalignment and damaged threads where a bolt must be placed. They also installed a camera on the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Space_Station\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:International Space Station\">International Space Station</a>'s robotic arm, Canadarm2. The bright sun is visible at left.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"8107641":{"pageid":8107641,"ns":6,"title":"File:NSB Di 4 Saltfjell.jpg","index":20,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":1489440,"width":4673,"height":2884,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/NSB_Di_4_Saltfjell.jpg/960px-NSB_Di_4_Saltfjell.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":960,"thumbheight":592,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/NSB_Di_4_Saltfjell.jpg/1920px-NSB_Di_4_Saltfjell.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/NSB_Di_4_Saltfjell.jpg/960px-NSB_Di_4_Saltfjell.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":960,"height":592,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/NSB_Di_4_Saltfjell.jpg/1920px-NSB_Di_4_Saltf